qca-ssdk: re-apply the uniphy forced speed after the port reset

adpt_mp_uniphy_mode_configure() sets ch0_force_speed in
UNIPHY_CHANNEL0_INPUT_OUTPUT_4 via adpt_mp_uniphy_mode_ctrl_set(), and
then calls adpt_mp_gcc_uniphy_port_reset() which power-cycles the uniphy
port.  That returns the register to its 0x844 reset default, clearing the
bit that was just set - confirmed by reading it back on cmcc,pz-l8, where
it holds exactly 0x844 with ch0_force_speed = 0 after a full init.

It only matters when the SGMII peer is forced too.  Here the peer is a
QCA8337 whose port 6 qca,ar8327-initvals forces to 1000/full, so it sends
no SGMII auto-negotiation code words while the uniphy waits for one:
both ends report a link up and no frame ever crosses the segment.  The
switch-side registers all read back exactly as programmed, and the
port 6 MAC counters increment on transmit, so the break is purely the
SerDes never completing.

Re-apply the setting once the port reset, calibration and clock enable
are all done.

--- a/src/adpt/mp/adpt_mp_uniphy.c
+++ b/src/adpt/mp/adpt_mp_uniphy.c
@@ -381,6 +381,35 @@
 		ssdk_mp_raw_clock_set(index + 1, UNIPHY_TX, clock);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Re-apply the forced-speed selection.
+	 *
+	 * adpt_mp_uniphy_mode_ctrl_set() above sets ch0_force_speed in
+	 * UNIPHY_CHANNEL0_INPUT_OUTPUT_4, but adpt_mp_gcc_uniphy_port_reset()
+	 * right after it power-cycles the uniphy port, which returns that
+	 * register to its 0x844 reset default and clears the bit again.
+	 *
+	 * When the SGMII peer is itself forced, nothing then brings the link up:
+	 * on cmcc,pz-l8 the peer is a QCA8337 whose port 6 is forced to
+	 * 1000/full by qca,ar8327-initvals, so it never sends SGMII
+	 * auto-negotiation code words, while the uniphy is left waiting for an
+	 * auto-negotiation that never arrives.  Both ends report a link and not
+	 * one frame is exchanged.
+	 */
+	if (hsl_port_feature_get(dev_id, SSDK_PHYSICAL_PORT2, PHY_F_FORCE)) {
+		union uniphy_channel0_input_output_4_u force_ctrl;
+
+		memset(&force_ctrl, 0, sizeof(force_ctrl));
+		rv = hppe_uniphy_channel0_input_output_4_get(dev_id, index,
+			&force_ctrl);
+		SW_RTN_ON_ERROR (rv);
+		force_ctrl.bf.newaddedfromhere_ch0_force_speed_25m =
+			UNIPHY_FORCE_SPEED_ENABLE;
+		rv = hppe_uniphy_channel0_input_output_4_set(dev_id, index,
+			&force_ctrl);
+		SW_RTN_ON_ERROR (rv);
+	}
+
 	if (mode == PORT_WRAPPER_SGMII_CHANNEL0) {
 		SSDK_DEBUG("mp uniphy %d sgmii configuration is done!\n", index);
 	} else {
